{"strongs": "H8414", "word": "תֹּ֫הוּ", "translit": "to.hu", "root": "תהה", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "formlessness, confusion, unreality, emptiness", "definition": "תֹּ֫הוּ noun masculine 1Sam 12:21 ( Albr ZAW xvi (1896), 112 ) formlessness, confusion, unreality, emptiness (primary meaning difficult to seize; Vrss usually Κενόν , οὐδέν , μάταιον , inane, vacuum, vanum ; compare Lag Or. ii. 60 ; BN 144); — 1. formlessness , of primaeval earth Gen 1:2 ( P ), of land reduced to primaeval chaos Jer 4:23 (both + וָבֹהוּ and voidness ), Isa 34:11 ׳ קַותֿֿ (|| אַבְנֵי בֹהוּ ), Isa 45:18 בְרָאָהּ ׳ לֹא ת (|| לָשֶׁבֶת יְצָרָתּ ); Isa 24:10 ׳ קִרְיַתאתּ city of chaos (of ruined city); = nothingness, empty space , Job 26:7 תֹּלֶה אֶרֶץ ׳ עַלתּֿ ; of empty, trackless waste Deut 32:10 (|| מִדְבָּר ), Job 6:18 ; Job 12:24 = Ps 107:40 . 2. figurative of what is empty, unreal , as idols 1Sam 12:21 (collective: אֲשֶׁר ׳ אַחֲרֵי הַתּ לֹא יוֺעִילוּ ), v 1Sam 12:21 ; Isa 41:29 נִסְכֵּיהֶם ׳ רוּחַ וָת , Isa 44:9 (of idol-makers), groundless arguments or considerations, Isa 29:21 צַדִּיק ׳ וַיַּטּוּ בַתּ , Isa 59:4 moral unreality or falsehood ׳ בָּטוֺחַ עַלאתּ (|| וְדַבֶּרשָֿׁוְא ); = a thing of nought (compare Eccl 41:10 מתהו אל תהו ), Isa 40:17 (|| אַיִן אֶפֶס ), v Isa 40:23 עָשָׂה ׳ שֹׁפְטֵי אֶרֶץ כַּתּ (|| לְאַיִן ), worthlessness Isa 49:19 וְהֶבֶל כֹּחִי כִלֵּיתִי ׳ לְת (|| לְרִיק יָגַעְתִּי ); as adverb accusative Isa 45:19 I said not, תֹּהוּ בַקְּשׁוּנִי seek me emptily, to no purpose. compare Isa 29:13 ᵐ5 וְתֹהוּ for וַתְּהִי .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB9112')\">BDB9112</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H8414')\">H8414</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB9111')\">BDB9111</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB9113')\">BDB9113</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>תֹּ֫הוּ</bdbheb> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"1Sam 12:21\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(9,12,21)\">1Sam 12:21</ref></sup> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Albr.')\">Albr<sup>ZAW xvi (1896), 112</sup></lookup>) <highlightword>formlessness, confusion, unreality, emptiness</highlightword> (primary meaning difficult to seize; <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Vrss')\"><reflink>Vrss</reflink></lookup> usually <grk>Κενόν</grk>, <grk>οὐδέν</grk>, <grk>μάταιον</grk>, <highlight>inane, vacuum, vanum</highlight>; compare <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Lag')\">Lag<sup>Or. ii. 60</sup></lookup>; BN 144); — <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> <highlight>formlessness</highlight>, of primaeval earth <ref ref=\"Gen 1:2\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(1,1,2)\">Gen 1:2</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('P')\"><reflink>P</reflink></lookup>), of land reduced to primaeval chaos <ref ref=\"Jer 4:23\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(24,4,23)\">Jer 4:23</ref> (both + <bdbheb>וָבֹהוּ</bdbheb> <highlight>and voidness</highlight>), <ref ref=\"Isa 34:11\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"34\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"34\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(23,34,11)\">Isa 34:11</ref> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>קַותֿֿ</bdbheb> (|| <bdbheb>אַבְנֵי בֹהוּ</bdbheb>), <ref ref=\"Isa 45:18\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"45\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"45\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(23,45,18)\">Isa 45:18</ref> <bdbheb>בְרָאָהּ</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>לֹא ת</bdbheb> (|| <bdbheb>לָשֶׁבֶת יְצָרָתּ</bdbheb>); <ref ref=\"Isa 24:10\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(23,24,10)\">Isa 24:10</ref> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>קִרְיַתאתּ</bdbheb> <highlight>city of chaos</highlight> (of ruined city); = <highlight>nothingness, empty space</highlight>, <ref ref=\"Job 26:7\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"26\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"26\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(18,26,7)\">Job 26:7</ref> <bdbheb>תֹּלֶה אֶרֶץ</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>עַלתּֿ</bdbheb>; of empty, trackless <highlight>waste</highlight> <ref ref=\"Deut 32:10\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(5,32,10)\">Deut 32:10</ref> (|| <bdbheb>מִדְבָּר</bdbheb>), <ref ref=\"Job 6:18\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(18,6,18)\">Job 6:18</ref>; <ref ref=\"Job 12:24\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"24\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"24\" onclick=\"bcv(18,12,24)\">Job 12:24</ref> = <ref ref=\"Ps 107:40\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"107\" vBegin=\"40\" cEnd=\"107\" vEnd=\"40\" onclick=\"bcv(19,107,40)\">Ps 107:40</ref>. </div><div class=\"point\"><b>2.</b> figurative of what is <highlight>empty, unreal</highlight>, as idols <ref ref=\"1Sam 12:21\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(9,12,21)\">1Sam 12:21</ref> (collective: <bdbheb>אֲשֶׁר</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>אַחֲרֵי הַתּ</bdbheb> <bdbheb>לֹא יוֺעִילוּ</bdbheb>), v<ref ref=\"1Sam 12:21\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(9,12,21)\">1Sam 12:21</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 41:29\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"41\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"41\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(23,41,29)\">Isa 41:29</ref> <bdbheb>נִסְכֵּיהֶם</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>רוּחַ וָת</bdbheb>, <ref ref=\"Isa 44:9\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"44\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"44\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(23,44,9)\">Isa 44:9</ref> (of idol-makers), groundless arguments or considerations, <ref ref=\"Isa 29:21\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"29\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"29\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(23,29,21)\">Isa 29:21</ref> <bdbheb>צַדִּיק</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>וַיַּטּוּ בַתּ</bdbheb>, <ref ref=\"Isa 59:4\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"59\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"59\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(23,59,4)\">Isa 59:4</ref> moral unreality or falsehood <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>בָּטוֺחַ עַלאתּ</bdbheb> (|| <bdbheb>וְדַבֶּרשָֿׁוְא</bdbheb>); = <highlight>a thing of nought</highlight> (compare <checkingNeeded/><ref ref=\"Eccl 41:10\" b=\"21\" cBegin=\"41\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"41\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(21,41,10)\">Eccl 41:10</ref> <bdbheb>מתהו